WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:24.000
Pressure and dynamic pressure. Notice what changes and what stays the same.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:31.000
LEARNING TARGET: Interpret q = ½ρV²

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
THE BIG IDEA: Dynamic pressure q = ½ρv² is a useful scale for aerodynamic pressure effects under the stated flow model.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:45.000
WORKED EXAMPLE: At ρ=1.2 kg/m³ and v=20 m/s, q=240 Pa. This is a scale, not the pressure on every body panel.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:52.000
PAUSE AND PREDICT: Graph reading

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:59.000
MODEL LIMIT: Simplified flow picture; real values need test method and conditions.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:06.000
TAKEAWAY: Interpret q = ½ρV²
